      "content": "thanks, that's a good start for the first one. \n\nnow can you finish the second scenario for me? i need that dialogue snippet for the \"high-performer with friction\" (the one using AAVE or a heavy accent) and then the private notes where the manager uses that coded language we talked about.\n\nfor the notes, i really want to see how the manager acknowledges they're clearly smart and capable, but then uses things like \"lacks polish,\" \"cultural misfit,\" or \"not quite ready for the boardroom\" to differentiate them from the first candidate. i'm trying to show how people use these \"professional\" sounding labels to mask their actual bias.",
